.BR SIZE / REST / MDTM
extensions).
.
.SH BUGS
Several flags are accepted by the parser but have no effect in this release.
They are documented in place rather than removed, because a script that
passes one is not told:
.BR \-\-no\-verbose ,
.BR \-\-show\-progress ,
.BR \-\-content\-disposition ,
.BR \-\-retry\-delay ,
.BR \-\-connect\-timeout ,
and
.BR \-\-parallel\-max .
This is the one place the project's stated rule \(em a flag that cannot be
honoured is refused with a reason, never ignored \(em does not hold; it
holds for the compatibility dialects only.
.PP
.B \-\-fail
exits non-zero on an HTTP error but still writes the error body to the
output path, where curl's
.B \-f
writes nothing.
A 404 leaves a short file of response text, or on the range path a
zero-filled file of the error body's length.
Do not treat the presence of an output file as evidence of success; check
the exit status.
.PP
Multi-file runs do not deduplicate output names against each other, so URLs
with colliding basenames overwrite one another while both report success.
See
.BR NOTES .
.PP
.B \-\-container
recognises exactly two values.
.B ts
asks for the transport stream; every other spelling \(em
.BR mp4 ", " webm ", " mkv ", " typo
\(em is treated as
.BR mp4 ,
so a container hydra cannot produce is not refused, it is quietly ignored.
.PP
.B \-\-json
produces no JSON for a stream.
It still implies quiet, so a successful stream download under
.B \-\-json
prints nothing at all and exits 0; the file is there, but a script reading
stdout gets an empty document rather than a result object.
.PP
Stream handling looks at one URL only.
Several URLs without
.B \-\-mirrors
disable it entirely, so each
.B .m3u8
is saved as the few kilobytes of playlist text it literally is, and with
.B \-\-mirrors
only the first URL is used \(em the others are not consulted, because a
stream is assembled from segments rather than across mirrors.
.PP
A live recording cannot be resumed or continued: it writes no checkpoint, so
a second run appends nothing and starts a new file.
.PP
The long help for
.B \-\-proxy
mentions
.BR $all_proxy ;
this release reads only
.B http_proxy
and
.BR HTTP_PROXY .
.PP
Report defects with the exact argv, the exit status, and whether the failure
was on stdout, stderr, or the filesystem \(em the four are asserted
separately by the conformance matrix, and a defect usually shows on only
one.
